    "The MMP delta changes the metal and the transformation at once. The model carries a transform-difference block, but the estimand is not the pure metal substitution response of the exact-ligand line.",
    "Pairs are built inside one (cell, paper, duration) so a paper offset cannot enter the observed delta; the cost is that pairs spanning two papers are not counted even when the core matches.",
    "The leak rule only excludes pairs whose predicted molecule was measured under a training metal. A shared core is the whole point of MMP and is deliberately not excluded.",
    "Ridge alpha is fixed at 1.0 and never tuned on the held-out metal; the feature block is standardised implicitly by the scale of MACCS bits, so alpha is not scale-free across feature sets.",
